        ("law-space", "Clear the law, room, and electrical plan first", '''<p>Home cultivation rules vary by jurisdiction, age, residence, plant status, household cap, visibility, access, property documents, and local code. In New York, adults 21+ may cultivate within current limits, plants must be secure and inaccessible to people under 21, and the state warns that overloading or misusing a circuit can lead to fire. OCM recommends qualified electrical inspection when service or intended equipment is in doubt.</p><p>A controller cannot approve the circuit, receptacle, grounding, wiring, breaker, extension, placement, moisture control, load combination, or building. Finish the <a href="../../guides/new-york-home-cannabis-grow-planner/">home-grow planner</a> and the <a href="../../guides/cannabis-home-fire-safety-plan/">home fire-safety plan</a> before adding automation.</p>'''),
